From ca89efced48cd25ce540d01d6f34732e54dab364 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:39:52 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 11/26] Sequencer: measure the external clock tempo over the
 last 8 beats.

ext_ticks keeps the time of each 24th tick in a ring of 8 beats (SEQ_EXT_BEATS).
At each beat, the tempo is the mean tick period since the oldest beat in the ring.
A change under 1/64 gets a smoothing of 1/4. A larger change takes the new mean at once.
The first beats use the old smoothing, with the block time divided by the ticks of the block.
A clock time-out clears the ring.
Reason: Bluetooth MIDI gives all the ticks of one connection event in one block.
Before, only the first tick of a block counted, and its period was the time since the last block.
Thus the measured tempo and the tempo kept at the time-out (MID-12) were wrong.
In the host test at 120 BPM with 7.5-30 ms bursts, the kept tempo was 116-127.
New host test: test_ext_tempo_ble in tests/host/seq_test.c (120, 93 and 140 BPM, 1-30 ms events, a tempo change).
