From 21e1f54ef79d273c11189f5a3f31e1582c051f97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:40:12 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 12/26] Sequencer: a Start that comes after a Stop in the same
 block starts the sequencer.

seq_stop clears an earlier Start or Continue request when it sets the Stop request.
seq_advance does the Stop first, then the Start or Continue that is still set.
Reason: Bluetooth MIDI gives all the messages of one connection event in one block.
Before, a Stop request cleared every Start and Continue request of the same block.
Thus Stop, then Start from Loopy Pro in one event left X0X stopped.
A Start, then a Stop in one block still stops X0X.
New host test: test_ext_transport_ble in tests/host/seq_test.c (Start, Stop, Continue, Stop + Start, Start + Stop).
---
 BEHAVIOR.md                  |  2 +-
 firmware/src/seq/sequencer.c |  9 +++++---
