From b8f8137187c094c2efaa3fb8e98af0950258a613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:40:21 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 13/26] Sequencer: the first clock tick after an internal start
 does not play a second step.

If the external clock starts while the sequencer plays on the internal clock, seq_advance stops the internal step timing.
The first tick is then tick 0 of the step that plays, and the next step comes after a full step of ticks.
Reason: a MIDI Start with no clock in the last 0.5 s starts X0X on the internal clock (LIM-11).
Bluetooth MIDI can give the first tick in a later connection event than the Start.
Before, that first tick played step 2 at once, so X0X played one step ahead of Loopy Pro.
A Start in the same block as a tick does not change: the first tick plays step 1.
New host test: the last part of test_ext_transport_ble in tests/host/seq_test.c (first tick 7.5 ms after Start, 16 steps in one bar, step 2 at tick 6).
