From 7c574e156c0f5ac61a61c927f1d7e3e666b10ce1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:14:17 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 22/26] Live recording: a hit records on the nearest step and
 does not sound twice.

seq_rec_step gives the next step after half of the step that plays.
On the internal clock, it uses the samples to the next step. On an external clock, it uses the ticks into the step.
On an external clock, a next step that its tick armed and that did not play yet is also the next step.
seq_rec_skip marks a live hit on a step that did not play yet on this pass.
fire_step reads the mark, and fire_drum and fire_bass do not sound that voice or that 303 note on this pass.
The MIDI note out of that step still goes out. The next step clears the mark, and Start, Stop and restart clear it too.
drum_key and bass_kbd in ui.c call seq_rec_skip after they write the step.
BEHAVIOR.md has the new rule REC-06.
Reason: before, an early hit went to the step before, and a hit just before the loop start went to the last step.
The owner approved this change on 2026-10-16 at 20:11 (+10).
Tests: seq_test test_rec_nearest (internal clock, external clock, 303) and rec_live_test test_drum_nearest (whole app).
Result on 5b9c416: rec_live_test test_drum_nearest has 3 failures, and seq_test does not compile (no seq_rec_skip). Result with this commit: all checks pass.
